Z||000000||reddog||10-05-2001||08:46 PM||||Hey guys, I have another dumb Wheel/tire question for you! I have already ordered 17" Street Rebel 783's <A HREF="http://WWW.kmcwheels.com/streetrebel.html#" TARGET=_blank>WWW.kmcwheels.com/streetrebel.html#</A>   along with 215/45/17 and 235/45/17 tires for the front and back. My question is; is anyone running 50 series tires on 17's, or is 45's as high a profile as you would want to go on a 17" rim. I want to fill in the space in the fender wells as much as possible.Your input would be greatly appreciated,also if you have any pics that would be very helpful<BR>Thanks, Reddog||||reg||5
Z||000001||fix||10-05-2001||09:02 PM||||on a 7 inch rim like that I don't think you'd be able to run a 50.  In fact I think you'd be pushing it by running a 45, but I don't really know that much about this.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rick 88||10-05-2001||09:09 PM||||I had a 255/45/17 trial mounted on the back of my 88 with 7.5 in wheels. It fit with no interference. It just looked to tall to me. I like the 215/245 combo I ended up with. It fills the fenders nicely.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wannabe||10-05-2001||09:14 PM||||235-45 is a tad snug on a 7" rim, but shouldn't be a problem. 50 series on 17's is definitely taller than oe.||||reg||1
